This scenario adapts Schnapp BH, Alvarez A, Bailey A, et al. (2018), "An Interactive Session to Help Faculty Manage
Difficult Learner Behaviors in the Didactic Setting", MedEdPORTAL 14:10774, doi:10.15766/mep_2374-8265.10774 (CC
BY-NC-SA 4.0), which allows non-commercial use only. It is one of the ten scenarios of the non-commercial subset
(`"nc": true` in benchmark/index.json); the rest of the benchmark's text is CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA) and the code is
MIT (LICENSE). The leaderboard includes these ten scenarios, so a commercial use of the benchmark has to leave them
out, and its scores are then not comparable with the leaderboard.

Changes: the source was adapted into a benchmark scenario; source.md gives the citation, the quoted passages and what
was adapted. The source's authors do not endorse this benchmark.
